    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d252">

                <pb facs="0237" n="165" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg165"/>

                <head>Teachers of the Ragged School</head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-01">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 1, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Honored Sir</hi>: We, the undersigned, teachers
                    connected with the Bristol ragged schools, beg permission to express through you
                    our unqualified indignation at the brutal act which has deprived America of one
                    of its best Presidents, and of the man especially adapted to the requirements of
                    the time.</p>
                <p>We venture to ask that you will kindly forward our condolence to Mrs. Lincoln,
                    who has been so barbarously bereaved of her illustrious husband.</p>
                <pb facs="0238" n="166" xml:id="pg166"/>
                <p>We earnestly pray that God will speedily restore peace to your united and great
                    country, and rescue it from the effects of a most wanton and wicked
                    rebellion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>JAMES SHEPPERLY, <hi rendition="#italic">Master</hi>.</item>
                            <item>MARTHA JANE HARWOOD, <hi rendition="#italic">Infant
                                Mistress</hi>.</item>
                            <item>JOHN ALLEN.</item>
                            <item>ELIZA OXBURGH.</item>
                            <item>LOUISA COOK.</item>
                            <item>RICHARD WEYMAN, <hi rendition="#italic">Tailor</hi>.</item>
                            <item>ELIZA PALMER.</item>
                            <item>JOSEPH PALMER.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">C. F. Adams</hi>, <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United States Minister</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
